\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The companion study's three evidence tests and their accuracies. Top: the three tests as drawn in the companion study's opening figure (Seidenberg Annual Research Day (SARD), Pace University, 11 December 2026), redrawn. Bottom: accuracy in the reference condition and in the changed-evidence condition. On WELFake, a TF-IDF support vector machine scores 96.5\% on cleaned text and 96.2\% after the ``Reuters'' cue is removed; on CIFAKE, a fine-tuned ResNet18 scores 96.3\% on clean images and 85.6\% after Gaussian blur at evaluation; on MMFakeBench, frozen LAYA-Vision scores 27.93\% with text alone and 26.42\% with image and text. These are the companion study's results, measured with frozen models; this paper's own results are in Section~\ref {sec:experiments}.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sard}{{1}{2}{The companion study's three evidence tests and their accuracies. Top: the three tests as drawn in the companion study's opening figure (Seidenberg Annual Research Day (SARD), Pace University, 11 December 2026), redrawn. Bottom: accuracy in the reference condition and in the changed-evidence condition. On WELFake, a TF-IDF support vector machine scores 96.5\% on cleaned text and 96.2\% after the ``Reuters'' cue is removed; on CIFAKE, a fine-tuned ResNet18 scores 96.3\% on clean images and 85.6\% after Gaussian blur at evaluation; on MMFakeBench, frozen LAYA-Vision scores 27.93\% with text alone and 26.42\% with image and text. These are the companion study's results, measured with frozen models; this paper's own results are in Section~\ref {sec:experiments}}{figure.1}{}}
