\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The CAL-1 calibration picture. A temperature fitted on the calibration split (choice \(T=8.4214\); the score and screen temperatures stayed at 1.0) improves ECE where it was fitted and on the tune split, then severely harms held-out validation calibration (0.1056 to 0.3955). A split-half fit on the held-out distribution itself (\(T=1.65\); a full-validation fit gives \(T=1.6\)) repairs it (0.0994 to 0.021). A same-distribution fit transfers; a training-distribution fit does not. Both published packs therefore ship at \(T=1.0\).}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cal1}{{6}{12}{The CAL-1 calibration picture. A temperature fitted on the calibration split (choice \(T=8.4214\); the score and screen temperatures stayed at 1.0) improves ECE where it was fitted and on the tune split, then severely harms held-out validation calibration (0.1056 to 0.3955). A split-half fit on the held-out distribution itself (\(T=1.65\); a full-validation fit gives \(T=1.6\)) repairs it (0.0994 to 0.021). A same-distribution fit transfers; a training-distribution fit does not. Both published packs therefore ship at \(T=1.0\)}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Supplementary-tier behaviour on the MMFakeBench tune split. (a) The data-size curve at 490 steps: performance collapses at 122 training items (0.1168), recovers at 245 items (0.3670), and reaches 0.6598 at 490 items. (b) The LoRA rank ladder under soft-ce: rank 8 and rank 16 remain trainable at both step budgets, while rank 32 collapses. The rank-16 column is the main grid's LoRA arm.}}{13}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ablations}{{7}{13}{Supplementary-tier behaviour on the MMFakeBench tune split. (a) The data-size curve at 490 steps: performance collapses at 122 training items (0.1168), recovers at 245 items (0.3670), and reaches 0.6598 at 490 items. (b) The LoRA rank ladder under soft-ce: rank 8 and rank 16 remain trainable at both step budgets, while rank 32 collapses. The rank-16 column is the main grid's LoRA arm}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The data-size curve on its own (supplementary tier, winner recipe at a fixed 490 steps). At 122 training items the model collapses to a single class (tune macro-F1 0.1168); 245 items give 0.3670 and 490 items give 0.6598. The 0.1168 value is shared, to full precision, with the rank-32 supplementary run at 490 steps: both runs collapse to the same single-class prediction pattern on the same tune split, so the identity is a shared collapse value, not a copying error.}}{13}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:datasize}{{8}{13}{The data-size curve on its own (supplementary tier, winner recipe at a fixed 490 steps). At 122 training items the model collapses to a single class (tune macro-F1 0.1168); 245 items give 0.3670 and 490 items give 0.6598. The 0.1168 value is shared, to full precision, with the rank-32 supplementary run at 490 steps: both runs collapse to the same single-class prediction pattern on the same tune split, so the identity is a shared collapse value, not a copying error}{figure.8}{}}
